+# satelle init --all --yes heals every registered repo whose stamp is behind a
+# breaking release, and init re-stamps before anything it runs can warn about
+# the old stamp
+
+Only a per-repo satelle init healed. Per the sync architecture the heal must
+reach every registered repo; slice sty_e0694a77 later makes satelle update run
+it.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. satelle init --all counts a registered repo as stale when its deployed stamp
+   is below the running binary, whether or not its scaffolding changed, and
+   --yes heals it exactly as a per-repo satelle init would, proven by a test
+   over a fixture registry with one repo behind a breaking release, one behind
+   a non-breaking release and one current.
+2. After satelle init --all --yes, no registered repo refuses a store-backed
+   command for a breaking-release stamp, proven by the same test running a
+   store-backed verb in each.
+3. Within satelle init, the stamp is written before any step that checks it, so
+   a single run prints no warning about the stamp it is replacing, proven by a
+   test capturing init's output for a repo behind a breaking release.
